        <briefdescription>
<para>computes water saturation from the mass balance; </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="attention"><para>use only if all 3 components are there</para>
</simplesect>
Calculates the volume fraction of water from the masses of the aqueous, carbonic and salt phase.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Vi = mass_i / density_i, the volume fraction is the phase volume over the total volume.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para>since precipitatated salt also occupies a fraction of the pore space, the water and carbondioxide saturations will be reduced correspondingly. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
